From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSI M4: close-out -- snapshot + determinism receipts

No production code was missing here, and the close-out proves it
rather than assuming it.  MSI/MSI-X state already rides the existing
snapshot composition: both controller structs go whole (dev.xhci,
dev.ahciN) and the Message Control bits ride the per-function
256-byte PCI config records.  v_msix_snapshot (test-xhci, last group
by necessity -- a load rewrites the machine) programmes entry 0 and
Enable, saves, vandalises the live state (disable, scribble the
entry, HCRST), loads, and asserts all three layers back: cfg bit,
table contents, and live delivery of the next message with the pin
silent.  test-msi gains the message-script determinism replay x2.

(The test-xhci link line gains src/snapshot.c for the save/load API.)

NC: MSI-X state dropped at snapshot load -> 3 failures.  Gates:
make test, make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

This closes the MSI plan (M0-M4, patches 0082-0086): QEMU-parity
MSI-X on the xHCI, an x86 delivery core on the proven LAPIC sink,
ICH-parity MSI on both AHCIs, edge routing with INTx fallback
preserved byte-for-byte, and snapshot/determinism receipts.
